        "title": "Audit and Controls - Trust, SOX, GAAP vs IFRS",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The financial statements are produced by the people they evaluate — an obvious incentive\nproblem. The trust infrastructure that makes external accounting credible has three layers:\n**standards** (GAAP/IFRS) define what \"correct\" means; **internal controls** (and SOX) make\nthe production process tamper-resistant; **audit** independently verifies the output. This is\nthe security model of accounting — threat model, controls, and an external verifier."
    }
